  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 212 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe upper level ridging continues to build northward from the \nSouthern Plains this weekend. This will bring a return to hot \ntemperatures. Sunday looks to have the potential to be exceptionally \nhot. LREF/Ensemble mean high temperatures are well over 100 \ndegrees and excessive heat headlines may be needed. Monday \ncontinues to look hot, but by Tuesday through Thursday, the \nridge sinks back across the Southern Plains. This will allow for\na return of several disturbances rotating around the high. \nMoisture content will remain high as sub-tropical moisture \ncontinues rotate north and then eastward across the region. This\nwill likely lead to an increase in showers and thunderstorms. \nWith the increased cloud cover, slightly cooler temperatures \nare expected with highs settling back into the lower to mid 90s.",
